# LC certification overhead accounting · `spec:nrz:lc-overhead-design`

**Decision (Formal accounting before measurement)** · `dec:nrz:lc-overhead-contract`

This design supplies the cost functionals, observation contract and fixed acceptance rule required by (`req:nrz:lc-overhead-acceptance-protocol`). It refines (`spec:nrz:lc-compute-concept`) and governs (`claim:nrz:lc-closing-naive-model`), (`claim:nrz:lc-closing-overhead-budget`), (`claim:nrz:lc-closing-overhead-tracking`), (`claim:nrz:lc-closing-overhead-bound`). It asserts no measurement, numerical enclosure proof or closing status change. The approximate four-to-eightfold prediction remains a budget to discharge; the acceptance bound is separate. There is no absolute latency gate (`dec:nrz:lc-resonance-delivery-contract`).

## Functionals and reference scope · `sec:nrz:lc-overhead-functionals`

**Definition (Frozen model instance)** · `def:nrz:lc-overhead-instance`

A question q specifies the original semantics, output form, scalar output count o, sample and branch selections, quantifier order and supported algorithm graph. An input family I specifies original source supports and dependencies, physical and index axes, occupied selections, endpoint/face candidates, exponent classes, tile partition, input representation and memory layout of arrived host arrays (stride, record width, alignment, padding, indirection), source versions and reuse lifetime. Use n for original instances, K for occupied numerical selections and E for actually examined selections; N below is a time functional, not a population. J and B are the actual requested sample and branch multiplicities of (`def:nrz:lc-compute-cell`). Record n,J,B,K,E separately, with K=n*J*B only for a dense product. Padded capacity is never K. First/last scans report both E and K; each naive graph uses its own deterministic exit on I and records its own examined count, which need not equal the certified E; matched per-cell ratios use the common K, while examined-cell costs retain their separate denominators; analytic aggregate references retain the cut/index shortcut of (`calc:nrz:lc-compute-aggregate-shortcut`). An empty domain has a question cost but no per-cell ratio. Lazy infinite aliases are priced only for the requested finite selections. The reference and certification answer the same q over I, including the same endpoints and face obligations, under (`def:nrz:lc-compute-components`).

**Definition (Documented machine parameters)** · `def:nrz:lc-overhead-machine`

Let theta contain core count p, clock f in cycles/second, binary64 lane width w, instruction operand classes, reciprocal throughput and latency, execution-resource eligibility, cache capacities and topology, load/store byte rates, memory traffic policy and bandwidth by level. Every numerical hardware coefficient requires a named document, revision and exact table/row; derived rates retain their derivation. Machine facts, host configuration readings and sourced or derived sensitivity assumptions are distinct fields; every speed-affecting parameter is subject to the reference floor, ceiling and manifest-wide configuration rule in (`rule:nrz:lc-overhead-host-configuration`), (`open:nrz:lc-overhead-machine-decision`). Configuration readings are not measured durations and do not calibrate the model. The source-record format is (`def:nrz:lc-overhead-source-record`); the supplied AMD arithmetic rows are mapped by (`obs:nrz:lc-overhead-amd-arithmetic`). The illustrative AMD sources and remaining unresolved assumptions are (`sec:nrz:lc-compute-machine-model`), (`hyp:nrz:lc-compute-throughputs`), (`hyp:nrz:lc-compute-bandwidth`). No measured duration, bandwidth, counter-derived rate, calibration or fitted intercept may set theta or the naive inventory (`rule:nrz:compute-model-boundary`). Unresolved coefficients remain symbolic and block a numerical acceptance verdict under (`open:nrz:lc-overhead-machine-decision`).

**Definition (Manufacturer source record)** · `def:nrz:lc-overhead-source-record`

A source of record names the compute vendor, processor family and applicable stepping/operand classes, document title, publication identifier, revision, artifact filename and cryptographic digest, sheet/table and row identifiers, original column names and units. It maps latency to the dependency graph, reciprocal throughput to resource demand, execution pipes to eligibility, and instruction width to lanes. Preserve the source values separately from conversion formulas, explicitly marking inferred units or applicability and any missing operand cases. The model is vendor-neutral: further manufacturer tables, including published Intel or Arm latency/throughput tables, can populate the same theta schema without changing N, C or the composition rule. Do not transfer coefficients between vendors or microarchitectures. Choice of a vendor-specific record and its unresolved applicability belongs to (`open:nrz:lc-overhead-machine-decision`).

**Observation (AMD arithmetic source mapping)** · `obs:nrz:lc-overhead-amd-arithmetic`

The source is AMD's [Software Optimization Guide for AMD Family 19h Processors, publication 56665, revision 3.00](https://docs.amd.com/v/u/en-US/56665) and its companion workbook `Family_19h_Instruction_Latencies_version_1-00.xlsx`, sheet `19h_latencies`, in archive `56665.zip`, SHA-256 `51f0b563d2fe2a706bf0148e49291c60f6679f0c272be312f114444ad3fe8492`. The original headers are Instruction, Op1, Op2, Op3, Op4, APM Vol, Cpuid flag, Ops, Unit, Latency and Throughput. The supplied extract preserves the following rows separately; it does not supply Op4 cell values, so none is inferred. Row 739: Instruction VADDPD, Op1 xmm1, Op2 xmm2, Op3 xmm3, APM Vol 4, Cpuid flag AVX, Ops 1, Unit FP2/3, Latency 3, Throughput 2. Row 740: Instruction VADDPD, Op1 ymm1, Op2 ymm2, Op3 ymm3, APM Vol 4, Cpuid flag AVX, Ops 1, Unit FP2/3, Latency 3, Throughput 2. Row 1097: Instruction VMULPD, Op1 xmm1, Op2 xmm2, Op3 xmm3, APM Vol 4, Cpuid flag AVX, Ops 1, Unit FP0/1, Latency 3, Throughput 2. Row 1098: Instruction VMULPD, Op1 ymm1, Op2 ymm2, Op3 ymm3, APM Vol 4, Cpuid flag AVX, Ops 1, Unit FP0/1, Latency 3, Throughput 2. Row 833: Instruction VFMADD132PD, Op1 xmm1, Op2 xmm2, Op3 xmm3, APM Vol 4, Cpuid flag FMA, Ops 1, Unit FP0/1, Latency 4, Throughput 2. Row 834: Instruction VFMADD132PD, Op1 ymm1, Op2 ymm2, Op3 ymm3, APM Vol 4, Cpuid flag FMA, Ops 1, Unit FP0/1, Latency 4, Throughput 2. Row 841: Instruction VFMADD213PD, Op1 xmm1, Op2 xmm2, Op3 xmm3, APM Vol 4, Cpuid flag FMA, Ops 1, Unit FP0/1, Latency 4, Throughput 2. Row 842: Instruction VFMADD213PD, Op1 ymm1, Op2 ymm2, Op3 ymm3, APM Vol 4, Cpuid flag FMA, Ops 1, Unit FP0/1, Latency 4, Throughput 2. Row 849: Instruction VFMADD231PD, Op1 xmm1, Op2 xmm2, Op3 xmm3, APM Vol 4, Cpuid flag FMA, Ops 1, Unit FP0/1, Latency 4, Throughput 2. Row 850: Instruction VFMADD231PD, Op1 ymm1, Op2 ymm2, Op3 ymm3, APM Vol 4, Cpuid flag FMA, Ops 1, Unit FP0/1, Latency 4, Throughput 2. Row 819: Instruction VDIVPD, Op1 xmm1, Op2 xmm2, Op3 xmm3, APM Vol 4, Cpuid flag AVX, Ops 1, Unit FP3, Latency 13, Throughput 0.15384615384615385. Row 820: Instruction VDIVPD, Op1 ymm1, Op2 ymm2, Op3 ymm3, APM Vol 4, Cpuid flag AVX, Ops 1, Unit FP3, Latency 13, Throughput 0.15384615384615385. Row 1455: Instruction VSQRTPD, Op1 xmm1, Op2 xmm2, Op3 blank, APM Vol 4, Cpuid flag AVX, Ops 1, Unit FP3, Latency 20, Throughput 0.1. Row 1456: Instruction VSQRTPD, Op1 ymm1, Op2 ymm2, Op3 blank, APM Vol 4, Cpuid flag AVX, Ops 1, Unit FP3, Latency 20, Throughput 0.1. Reading Latency as core cycles and Throughput as instructions per core-cycle is an inference from these values and pipe multiplicities, not a quoted unit definition from the workbook's bare headers. Under that explicit interpretation, divide throughput is approximately 2/13 and rho_div=13/2, while rho_sqrt=10 cycles per vector; add, multiply and FMA each have reciprocal throughput 1/2. The xmm operands have 128-bit width and two binary64 lanes; the ymm operands have 256-bit width and four binary64 lanes. These arithmetic rows provide the arithmetic coefficients under the stated interpretation; they do not establish comparisons, mask extraction, integer packing, sustainable bandwidth, exceptional operands or all mixed-pipe schedules. FP3 is shared by divide/root and is also eligible for add; a schedule must respect that overlap rather than treating these units as independent. The reference Zen 3 family applicability is retained from (`sec:nrz:lc-compute-machine-model`); it is not an assertion that every Family 19h processor shares all other parameters.

**Definition (Resource demand and phase cost)** · `def:nrz:lc-overhead-resource`

For a legal instruction graph g in a sequential phase h, let v_h=(A,M,F,D,S,comparisons,floor,conversion,integer,mask,bytes_read,bytes_written) include actual vector instruction counts and scalar tails alongside scalar-equivalent counts. For fully occupied strips, vector count is scalar count divided by w; partial strips use actual executed vectors and active-lane counts, not fractional occupancy as if inactive lanes were free. Let d_hr be the total cycles demanded on resource r under an assignment a of instructions to eligible pipes, including shared occupancy. For N, choose the minimum-makespan legal assignment for each graph and phase, minimizing the binding resource demand jointly rather than minimizing each pipe independently; for C^pred, use the declared certified assignment. Retain the assignment and its optimality justification for N. Loads and stores contribute to their ports; memory-level traffic b_hl includes write allocation, rereads and eviction where required. Define H_theta(g,h;a)=max(max_r d_hr/(p_h*f), max_l b_hl/B_hl, L_h), in seconds, with L_h the dependency critical path and p_h equal to the physical cores allotted to the certified acceptance run for that phase, with the same allotment for N and C^pred. This allotment is the parallelism ceiling, never the whole node's core count; serial dependencies remain in L_h. The primary single-core runs use p_h=1; any separately required parallel question freezes its phase allotments and affinity in the manifest, justifies the chosen core count p_h for each phase under (`rule:nrz:lc-overhead-precollection-review`), and uses those same allotments on both sides. Shared node bandwidth is not multiplied by cores. A phase's legal schedule and traffic assumptions determine whether this throughput estimate is admissible; it is not a worst-case runtime guarantee.

**Definition (Optimized naive cost)** · `def:nrz:lc-overhead-naive`

Let G(q,I) be the documented legal uncertified binary64 graphs from (`sec:nrz:lc-compute-naive`), (`sec:nrz:lc-compute-tiles`), including axis hoisting, reciprocal reuse, supported analytic reductions, recurrence reseeding and scaling. Define N_theta(q,I)=min_g sum_h min_a H_theta(g,h;a), for g in G(q,I) and legal eligible-pipe assignments a, with sequential setup, steady phases and finish all included. This is the minimum among the explicitly inventoried supported graphs, not a claim of global algorithmic optimality; inventory every applicable supported graph at full lane width w, with actual tails, and justify any excluded cheaper applicable graph before freezing G. Completeness of G, the full-width inventories, optimality of the eligible-pipe assignments, completeness of the admitted speed-affecting machine parameters, the sources or derivations of every sensitivity case, and completeness and case makeup of the acceptance manifest under (`req:nrz:lc-overhead-runs`), (`def:nrz:lc-overhead-case-makeup`), including the remaining producer choices in (`rule:nrz:lc-overhead-precollection-review`), are mandatory items for the independent closing review (`rule:nrz:lc-closing-independent-review`); the producer cannot establish these by declaration alone. Shared preparation is included once, and caches/reuse cannot be assumed across invalidating source versions. The full operation, byte and vector inventory accompanies the minimum. Report the binding resources and sensitivity to theta. The scalar expression for forward phase remains that of (`claim:nrz:lc-closing-naive-model`); no naive program is built or timed.

**Definition (Certified cost and ratio)** · `def:nrz:lc-overhead-certified`

C_theta^pred(q,I) is the predicted time of the selected certified graph, with its center/reference work and all certification components composed by (`rule:nrz:lc-overhead-composition`). C(q,I;z) is the elapsed seconds of one complete certified execution under recorded environment and observation configuration z; its estimated primary value is the host-sampling slope C_hat. Define R^pred=C_theta^pred/N_theta and R_hat=C_hat/N_theta with the same scope and strictly positive N_theta. A component's unique predicted factor is its ordered incremental time under (`def:nrz:lc-overhead-component-factor`) divided by that same N_theta, never a ratio to its own favorable subkernel. Measured factors use independently identifiable component time divided by N_theta; unresolved fused constituent factors remain unresolved under (`open:nrz:lc-overhead-fused-attribution`). Total C includes engine preparation, all attempts, validation, publication and mandatory release belonging to q; harness-only reset, receipt export and statistical analysis are separately recorded sampler costs. Consumer waits and external input arrival are separately identified and excluded only when the frozen q excludes them on both sides.

**Rule (Scopes and shared-work allocation)** · `rule:nrz:lc-overhead-scopes`

Report setup, steady state and finish separately and their full sum. Per-question costs are those sums; per-tile costs allocate shared preparation plus that tile's own work; per-cell costs divide matched totals by actual K, or by E with an explicit examined-cell designation. Per-cell R equals the corresponding total ratio only when both totals use the same divisor; separate naive and certified examined counts do not define a matched ratio (`def:nrz:lc-overhead-instance`). Averaging tile ratios does not produce the question ratio. Allocate an axis producer, pi import, branch coefficient, exact cache construction or shared barrier among its actual consuming tiles with weights a_ut proportional to the number of dependency uses in each tile, with sum_t a_ut=1. Record the use graph and retain producer totals independently; the allocated views are not additional charges. If a producer has no consumer, retain it in setup/waste rather than dividing by zero. Empty and partial tiles, failed/refused attempts, eviction, rebuilding, reseeding and exponent scaling retain their actual costs. Every required (q,I) has a mandatory cold full-question instance, starting in a fresh process or after a demonstrated reset of all such state, including process-lifetime static tables and caches, without retained constructed authority, pi evidence, prepared plans or built caches; its C includes their construction and all setup and finish. Warm runs require declared eligible retained authority and are additional distinct instances, never substitutes for cold acceptance. A changing reuse horizon changes I and invalidates the old denominator (`open:nrz:lc-compute-attribution`).

## Components and composition · `sec:nrz:lc-overhead-components`

**Definition (Center and ordinary execution)** · `def:nrz:lc-overhead-center`

The center component contains the certified graph's numerical center instructions, ordinary input loads, loop infrastructure and required reference output bytes. Its prediction starts from the selected naive inventory, but any certified reassociation restriction or extra center computation is stated explicitly; it is not silently set equal to N. Counters distinguish A,M,F,D,S and ordinary input/output bytes. Center-plane stores belong here; decision-map and coverage-mask stores belong wholly to the mask component, so no reference mask write is also charged here. Assign shared loop/index instructions to one recorded owner before using the concept’s full integer schedule. The following components partition the remaining demand vectors, not independently additive roofline times; the mask component includes the reference mask write as well as certification additions.

**Definition (Radius term)** · `def:nrz:lc-overhead-radius`

The radius component propagates physical total radius and the separate numerical-only companion without adding the numerical error twice. Its schedule is (`calc:nrz:lc-compute-radius`): product propagation per channel is three M plus two A, or one M plus two F; addition adds A, and an FMA adds the third-input radius. The prepared-phase example uses (2,2,4,0,0) for both channels. Root and reciprocal variants retain their explicit S,D or prepared-bound multiplication inventory. Prediction is that vector times its actual operation multiplicities, with companion input traffic sixteen extra bytes per varying scalar before reuse. Required counters split channel, operation kind and bytes; source interaction terms absent from the provisional law are required extra demand, not an unexplained discount.

**Definition (Rounding term)** · `def:nrz:lc-overhead-rounding`

The rounding component selects one proven enclosure recipe per rounded operation from (`calc:nrz:lc-compute-rounding`): two M plus A per independently maintained channel for the a-priori schedule, or F plus residual accumulation for an error-free product, or six A plus accumulation for TwoSum. The prepared-phase two-channel example adds (2,4,0,0,0). Preparation of outward coefficients is shared setup. Subnormal allowance, roots, division and exceptional scaling retain their own proof and counts. Counters name recipe, channel, rounded operations and exceptional lanes; no rounding-mode switching is admitted.

**Definition (Cycle and decision term)** · `def:nrz:lc-overhead-decision`

The comparison component uses (`calc:nrz:lc-compute-membership`): two A form shared endpoints, two comparisons implement one threshold test, and up to four additional comparisons implement the cycle faces. Wrapping adds the enclosed turn multiple and subtraction for each output. Reused endpoints are charged once. Counters distinguish endpoint formation, threshold comparisons, face comparisons, branch import and wrapping operations; boundary/refinement frequency is an actual count. Exact pi construction belongs to the exact component, not to each face test.

**Definition (Mask and integer term)** · `def:nrz:lc-overhead-mask`

The mask component uses (`calc:nrz:lc-compute-certified-bytes`): c_integer_cert=4*c_pack+c_intersect+c_select+c_loadmask+c_other for the illustrated four result roles, with symbolic coefficients until the instruction schedule is documented. Three input masks and four output masks transfer 7/8 byte per full selection before padding; input intersection uses two wordwise AND operations per full word. Each independently stored mask uses 8*ceil(K_tile/64) bytes. Counters record role, words visited, intersections, extraction/packing, Boolean selection, safe masked loads or bounded packing, active lanes and padded lanes. Broadcast singleton coverage is charged once per reuse scope. Extra refusal/filled roles, sparse traversal and mask copies are explicit additions. Ordinary loop work already in the center component is not charged again.

**Definition (Companion output term)** · `def:nrz:lc-overhead-output`

The output component adds eight bytes per scalar for a total-radius plane and another eight for the numerical-only plane: 24o bytes versus 8o for a full three-plane reading, under (`calc:nrz:lc-compute-certified-bytes`). It counts stores, memory-level traffic and allocation/publication work, with mask stores retained in the mask component. Decision/aggregate kernels may retire transient companions without materializing them; retained intermediates and consumer rereads cost their actual bytes. Counters distinguish center, total-radius and numerical-only planes and written/read/released bytes. The approximately threefold memory-bound case is conditional on all arithmetic and mask demand fitting that memory term.

**Definition (Amortized exact term)** · `def:nrz:lc-overhead-exact`

The exact component inventories construction, pi evidence, cache key construction/lookup, proof, replay, branch coefficients, refinement and failed attempts at their owner scope. Predict its operation vector x_t from the selected exact recipe, precision, operand lengths and hit/miss schedule; predict time T_t(theta,x_t) by the same documented resource and dependency model, retaining symbolic operation costs where missing. For k occupied consumers the disjoint allowance is T_t/k, plus f_fallback*T_fallback for the fallback fraction fixed by the case construction in (`def:nrz:lc-overhead-case-makeup`); retain the actual fraction and reconcile any departure, never choose a smaller fraction to dilute saturated fallback cases. The eightfold local allowance is T_t<=k*t_naive*(8-R_kernel) only when the right side is nonnegative (`pred:nrz:lc-compute-overhead-envelope`). No measured exact cost may be substituted into a prior prediction. Native intervals retain an observed zero exact-Work receipt; rejected charges add no fictional consumption. Counters keep the existing exact Work dimensions and construction/cache/proof/replay counts without changing tariffs or pins.

**Definition (Target and layout validation term)** · `def:nrz:lc-overhead-validation`

Per-tile validation authenticates actual target/source versions, companion correspondence, mask layout, coverage and checked expansion before application; it does not repeat the full exact proof per cell (`crit:nrz:lc-compute-avoidable`). Predict V_t=sum_v n_v*d_v using the required version comparisons, layout checks, mask words and descriptor reads, with d_v a documented instruction/resource vector. Thus its amortized demand is V_t/k; no numerical constant is asserted by the concept. Counters name target/version checks, layout edges, coverage words, descriptor bytes and rejected attempts. Proof rechecking, when genuinely required after invalidation, goes to the exact term and remains visible.

**Rule (Resource sums before time sums)** · `rule:nrz:lc-overhead-composition`

Within a fused phase, sum component demand vectors by resource and memory level before applying H_theta. An instruction is assigned to exactly one component; a shared instruction has a recorded allocation whose fractions sum to one. Integer, vector logical and mask-extract instructions that use floating pipes add to that floating resource's demand; max(FP,integer) is valid only for documented separate resources. Divide and square-root occupancy add on their shared unit. Overlapped compute and memory use the binding maximum, while disjoint prelude, validation, barriers, fallback and finish add in elapsed time. For parallel work, use the dependency schedule and shared bandwidth, not the sum of worker wall times. Report marginal resource demands and binding-resource changes; do not sum independently computed component ratios. The conditional 4.25–8.5 local range in (`pred:nrz:lc-compute-overhead-envelope`) is neither a full-question prediction nor valid under arbitrary resource sharing.

**Definition (Ordered component factors)** · `def:nrz:lc-overhead-component-factor`

Freeze the attribution order before data: center, radius, rounding, comparison, mask, output, exact, validation, then any separately labelled additional components in a manifest-fixed order. Every predicted instruction, traffic charge and dependency duration, including sequential setup, barriers, included waits and finish, must have a frozen component owner before forming prefixes; no unowned predicted phase may be omitted. This prediction ownership does not change an explicit U assignment in (`req:nrz:lc-overhead-map`). Retain each owner's separately identified sequential barrier and included-wait prediction in the total predicted factor, but exclude that part from the owner's measured-component comparison and compare it against the corresponding U-assigned intervals instead; this diagnostic comparison does not reclassify U as accounted time or relax its limit. For each phase h, let H_h(S_i) be its modeled time with the first i components retained, using the declared certified resource assignment, traffic allocation and dependency schedule restricted to those components; H_h(empty)=0. Assign delta_hi=H_h(S_i)-H_h(S_previous) and factor F_i=sum_h delta_hi/N_theta. The order, ownership of shared instructions, traffic and dependencies, and restriction rule are frozen with the prediction; no reoptimization or change of overlap is allowed between prefixes. These ordered marginals are a unique accounting convention and sum to C_theta^pred/N_theta even when a component adds no binding time. They are not independently measured durations or a causal estimate of deleting a component. Compare them to measured component factors only where the required observable is identifiable under (`rule:nrz:lc-overhead-isolation`); joint fused evidence alone leaves constituent tracking unresolved.

## Observation and reconciliation · `sec:nrz:lc-overhead-observation`

**Requirement (Deterministic component receipts)** · `req:nrz:lc-overhead-counters`

Use the fixed spans and ledger-interval reconciliation of (`sec:nrz:tiles-streams-observability`), including causal identity, family, recipe revision, question, tile, attempt, source versions and ledger incarnation. Existing exact Work remains the sole charged budget; new native instruction/byte/occupancy counters are deterministic observation receipts alongside Work, not new Work tariffs. They count executed semantic operations from the actual path and independently reconcile to the selected recipe; they do not infer instruction lowering or physical cache misses from elapsed time. Instruction selection requires a retained lowering audit; bytes by cache/memory level are modeled unless independently observed and explicitly identified as such. Logical plane bytes are exact. A missing private ledger, open interval or observer loss makes the receipt incomplete, never zero.

**Requirement (Component measurement map)** · `req:nrz:lc-overhead-map`

The center, radius, rounding and comparison receipts attach to `nrz.kernel` with component and channel fields and the counters in (`def:nrz:lc-overhead-center`), (`def:nrz:lc-overhead-radius`), (`def:nrz:lc-overhead-rounding`), (`def:nrz:lc-overhead-decision`). Masks attach to `nrz.mask` events inside that kernel or a separate ordinary mask pass, with (`def:nrz:lc-overhead-mask`) counters. Output stores attach to their actual kernel; publication and lifetime events attach to `nrz.publish`, `nrz.memory`, `nrz.flush` and `nrz.retire`, with (`def:nrz:lc-overhead-output`) counters. Exact receipts attach to `nrz.prepare`, `nrz.prelude`, `nrz.lookup`, `nrz.proof`, `nrz.replay`, `nrz.refine` and finer `nrz.work.phase` boundaries, using (`def:nrz:lc-overhead-exact`). Validation attaches to `nrz.validation` and `nrz.layout`, using (`def:nrz:lc-overhead-validation`). The remaining fixed phases of (`def:nrz:tiles-streams-spans`) are assigned as follows: `nrz.lower` and `nrz.walk` to center, `nrz.loan`, `nrz.handback` and `nrz.deliver` to output, and `nrz.barrier` and `nrz.wait` explicitly to U. Exact construction, pi and cache receipts use `nrz.construct`, `nrz.pi` and `nrz.cache` under the exact owner; native construction events instead follow the center, mask or output owner of the constructed object. Events are counters attached to an owning span, never independent elapsed regions. Barrier and wait durations remain visible against the prior sequential schedule prediction but cannot become accounted component time without a separately labelled component and prior prediction. Host row, iteration and entered-interval identities join elapsed intervals to these receipts from the same execution; foreign-ledger transfers are reconciled once, not subtracted as same-ledger children.

**Requirement (Missing instrumentation is implementation work)** · `req:nrz:lc-overhead-additions`

Existing projected-ledger and host-collection controls cited by (`claim:nrz:lc-closing-cost-accounting`) do not provide the full LC map. Add LC recipe/component/channel identities, semantic A,M,F,D,S and comparison/conversion counters, vector/active/tail counts, per-role mask operations, per-plane logical traffic, version/layout validation counts, exact recipe and cache-event linkage, and observation-to-host-row correlation wherever absent. Extend coverage to failed, private-ledger and native zero-Work routes, including per-tile `nrz.validation` coverage where only prepared-function validation exists. Add `nrz.validation` to the fixed phase span vocabulary as a named per-tile validation span; its prepared-function use does not make it part of (`def:nrz:tiles-streams-spans`). The other generic span names are reused; this document does not claim these LC fields or counters already exist. The implementation must demonstrate that receipts are complete without changing arithmetic, existing Work or pins.

**Rule (Isolation without a replacement workload)** · `rule:nrz:lc-overhead-isolation`

Record counters at natural kernel/tile boundaries and sample whole ordinary operations; do not insert a timer or subscriber event per arithmetic operation, disable certification, subtract an ablation run or reconstruct the operation in a scalar microbenchmark. Nested spans produce exclusive elapsed time only for sequential disjoint regions. A fused center/radius/rounding/comparison/in-kernel-mask-packing/output-store kernel has one measured joint time and separately observed operation vectors; its component times are not independently identifiable from those vectors. Report each constituent time as unresolved within the joint interval, cite the joint measurement on each constituent, and count that joint region once in reconciliation. Do not call a model-proportional split a measured time. Independent component timing requires an existing separable ordinary region or the further decision in (`open:nrz:lc-overhead-fused-attribution`); unresolved attribution cannot substantiate the register's every-component measurement claim. Enabled-observer cost remains inside C; compare enabled and disabled configurations for diagnostic perturbation only, with semantic and Work equivalence, retaining both and never subtracting a presumed observer cost.

**Definition (One observation and elapsed accounting)** · `def:nrz:lc-overhead-observation`

One observation is one host-sampler row (k_j,t_j) for a fixed q,I,theta, scope and observation configuration, plus every constituent iteration's outcome, receipts and vector of exclusive measured region durations. k_j counts complete operations; t_j is the sum of their measured durations under (`rule:nrz:host-sampling-repetition`). Warm-up is separate and cannot prepare the retained state of a cold iteration. Each k_j operation in a cold row performs its own full-question construction and teardown; the prepared-plan reuse of (`rule:nrz:host-sampling-repetition`) applies only to separately declared warm observations. Each cold iteration starts in a fresh process or uses a demonstrated reset covering process-lifetime state, including static pi tables and exact caches. Harness reset restores those cold preconditions and cannot perform any question-owned construction outside t_j; question-owned process initialization remains inside t_j. For a parallel question, the model and certified run share the phase core allotments in (`def:nrz:lc-overhead-resource`); wall-time components must partition the root's elapsed timeline by the frozen causal schedule; overlapping worker intervals remain diagnostic work-time, not additive wall-time. If that partition cannot be observed, mark wall attribution incomplete. Retain setup, waits, finalization, failures and stop status; a stopped prefix is not a complete row. The scale observation executes its full declared population and consumes its requested outputs, not a representative tile multiplied by K.

**Definition (Measured remainder)** · `def:nrz:lc-overhead-remainder`

Let M_jg be the measured exclusive time of a disjoint component-owned span region g in (`req:nrz:lc-overhead-map`) with a frozen component prediction, including joint fused regions only once and the center region as well as overhead. Only those mapped component regions qualify. The root's and unmapped container spans' own time, other unmapped regions and explicitly U-assigned phases go to U. A mapped component span retains its own exclusive time in that component even when it contains child spans; children follow their own mapping. An enclosing span cannot absorb U-assigned intervals into a component; missing prediction or ownership is not a zero-cost component. Define U_j=t_j-sum_g M_jg and A_j=sum_g M_jg. U is the unexplained elapsed remainder, not a new predicted component and not an adjustable balancing allocation. Its signed value and the normalized fractions u=U/C and a=A/C are reported with absolute seconds and U/N. Negative U exposes overlap, broken boundaries or clock error; it is not clamped. Unclassified orchestration, scheduling and observer cost remain in U unless independently observed as a named additional component with a prior prediction. Resource-model residuals within measured fused regions are reported separately; a small U does not explain those residuals or resolve constituent attribution.

## Frozen acceptance protocol · `sec:nrz:lc-overhead-acceptance`

**Decision (Numerical tolerance and primary statistic)** · `dec:nrz:lc-overhead-threshold`

For (`req:nrz:lc-overhead-acceptance-protocol`), fix the allowed ratio at 10.0: numerical tolerance above ten is zero. Approximation belongs to the declared theoretical model, not an extra adjustable margin. This preserves the approximate 4–8 prediction and its headroom to ten without redefining either. Decide on the upper confidence endpoint of the certified elapsed-time slope divided by the frozen positive N_theta; neither a minimum time, median, point estimate nor favorable local ratio decides acceptance. Report both full-question and matched steady-state ratios; both must satisfy the bound for every (q,I) in the frozen manifest, each a required instance under (`req:nrz:lc-overhead-runs`). Setup and finish cannot disappear into a steady-state pass. The cold full-question instance is mandatory at every population required by (`req:nrz:lc-overhead-runs`); no amortization cutoff or warm-only manifest can exempt it.

**Decision (Intervals and comparisons fixed in advance)** · `dec:nrz:lc-overhead-intervals`

Before collection freeze the finite acceptance manifest and let m be its number of required ratio and remainder comparisons, including every scope and independent run. Use two-sided percentile bootstrap intervals of level 1-0.05/m, with the through-origin slope and paired row resampling of (`rule:nrz:host-sampling-estimates`). At least three independent runs per instance and at least ten complete rows per run are required; the actual row count, warm-up, seed, count caps, time budget and tracing configuration are frozen before collection. Use at least max(10000,ceil(400*m/0.05)) resamples so the expected count in each adjusted tail is at least two hundred. These are acceptance-host settings, not engine defaults. Resample entire row vectors together, retaining k_j,t_j and every M_jg, so component sums and U preserve covariance; do not combine marginal component intervals as if independent. Each run must pass; do not pool away drift. Keep chronological rows and all outliers. Additionally require every complete observed row to satisfy t_j/(k_j*N_theta)<=10.0 for the full-question scope, including cold rows, and t_j_steady/(k_j*N_theta_steady)<=10.0 for the matched steady-state scope, in every run. Here t_j_steady is the sum of the measured steady-region durations in that row and N_theta_steady is the corresponding theoretical steady-state time per operation; neither steady quantity includes setup or finish. The budget step records the resampling cost: for an illustrative manifest with m=10000 comparisons, the formula requires 80000000 resamples per interval. With only ten rows, such extreme percentile tails are effectively governed by the observed row extremes, so additional resampling does not add independent observations. Estimate analysis time and storage from the frozen m and row counts before collection; this is a budget risk, not permission to reduce the manifest, resample count or row guard. This distribution-free observed-row guard is mandatory even if the bootstrap endpoint passes; it asserts no population or future-run coverage. The union-bound adjustment targets nominal family error of 5% only if the individual intervals have their nominal coverage; percentile bootstrap coverage is approximate, may under-cover with ten rows and extreme adjusted tails, and is not guaranteed by increasing resamples. Neither this adjustment nor the row guard establishes a distribution-free confidence bound for unseen executions; retain the representativeness and stability prerequisites and report this coverage limitation plainly.

**Decision (Remainder limit)** · `dec:nrz:lc-overhead-remainder-limit`

For each bootstrap resample compute the signed ratio u_hat=(C_hat-sum_g M_hat_g)/C_hat using slopes from the same resampled rows and positive C_hat. Its entire adjusted interval must lie within [-0.01,0.01]; equivalently max(abs(lower),abs(upper))<=0.01. Also require the original point estimate to lie in that band and investigate any negative remainder as an accounting diagnostic. Thus unexplained time is at most one percent of measured total, or at most 1/99 of accounted time for a positive remainder at the limit. This is small relative to both the explained cost and the gap between the predicted budget and ten; it cannot excuse unexplained component departures. Signed cancellation across separately identified missing/overlapping regions is prohibited: incomplete coverage or invalid partitions fail reconciliation before the numerical test.

**Requirement (Acceptance manifest and actual scale)** · `req:nrz:lc-overhead-runs`

Map every question in (`def:nrz:lc-compute-questions`) and every required recipe in (`sec:nrz:lc-grid-acceptance`), (`req:nrz:lc-grid-benchmark`) to a frozen q,I inventory and machine evidence. Enumerate value maps, decisions, aggregates and first/last forms wherever the question definition supplies that form, cell/region quantifiers, sample and alias extents, finite-face V,H, calibrated futures, rational-square controls, ordinary nonsquare inputs, boundary/uncertain/refused cases, correlated supports and exhausted-refinement strata, with the case makeup and saturated instances of (`def:nrz:lc-overhead-case-makeup`). Keep the driven plan in its own scope. Use the pinned release binary64 single-core timing environment of (`req:nrz:lc-grid-benchmark`), both supported formats for correctness, and fixed sample/branch/output extents in the primary sweep, varying them separately. Execute every enumerated form at the smallest dense K at or above each power of ten from ten through 10⁹, reporting n, K and E, plus the original baseline slices. Each required population counts K, the occupied numerical selections defined in (`def:nrz:lc-overhead-instance`). Every (q,I) in the frozen manifest is a required instance subject to the ratio bound, including each enumerated form at every population, every separately varied sample, branch and output extent, and every original baseline slice; each has its own mandatory cold full-question run. Applicability is settled by the cited question definition, never by producer classification as scalable or convenient; record that definition and its implication for each inapplicable form. No otherwise applicable combination is excluded by this design; any exclusion requires a named amendment to this design with its reason before freezing the manifest. Mark unsupported combinations explicitly instead of substituting an easier question: any unsupported mark on an enumerated combination leaves (`claim:nrz:lc-closing-overhead-bound`) unmet, as does omission from the manifest. Manifest completeness and makeup require independent review before collection under (`rule:nrz:lc-overhead-precollection-review`) and at closing under (`def:nrz:lc-overhead-naive`); there is no small-population exemption. The budget step evaluates the cold full-question case at the smallest dense K at or above ten early, including exact construction and pi evidence, and reports its risk under (`rule:nrz:lc-overhead-verdict`). Include an ordinary positive L by C grid with 25000 by 40000 original instances, J=B=1 and nonsquare products, giving exactly 10⁹ cells, with reproducible axes and source associations. This shape is an acceptance fixture, not a tile default. Report n, K and E for every instance and every stop. Projection, early-exit E smaller than the required dense scale, or a smaller-size fit cannot supply the billion-cell evidence (`claim:nrz:lc-closing-scale-measurement`).

**Definition (Case makeup and saturation)** · `def:nrz:lc-overhead-case-makeup`

Each enumerated case form in (`req:nrz:lc-overhead-runs`), including the forms inherited from (`req:nrz:lc-grid-benchmark`), has a frozen construction specifying the share and placement of occupied selections, source/dependency structure, operand and exponent classes, boundary distance, exact operand lengths, refinement depth and stopping policy, fallback fraction, cache-hit/miss schedule and output obligations. For every applicable question/form and every required population, include a dense saturated instance with K=n*J*B in which that case fills every occupied selection. For each power of ten in (`req:nrz:lc-overhead-runs`), use the smallest dense K at or above that power, reporting n, K and E. Sparse occupancies are permitted only as additional representative instances with their named source or explicit derivation. Both saturated and representative instances are required and subject to both ratio scopes. A mixed case does not replace its separate saturated constituents. Omitting a saturated density requires a named amendment to this design with its reason before freezing, and an explicit exclusion in the claim's input scope; producer-declared rarity is not an exemption.

Rational-square controls fill every occupied selection with positive square-product inputs; ordinary nonsquare cases fill them with positive nonsquare products. Cycle, branch and threshold boundary cases separately place every occupied selection on the relevant face, with exact equality as its own saturated case. Uncertain cases give every occupied selection physical supports straddling the relevant decision boundary; refused cases make every selection exercise the specified refusal route, retaining its construction and attempted work. Exhausted-refinement cases make every occupied selection reach the applicable unchanged refinement limit without discharging its obligation; freeze that limit, the depth reached and fallback behavior rather than selecting an easier early stop. Correlated cases put every occupied selection in the declared joint-source dependency structure, recording grouping and correlation law; quiescent/rest cases fill the occupied domain with the relevant rest conditions. Alias and finite-face cases apply the declared alias extent and V,H obligations to every selection; calibrated-future cases apply the same declared calibration and horizon obligations throughout. Cached-authority cases make every selection consume the declared authority, with construction included in cold scope; miss cases require every selection to miss the declared cached domain, including values beyond precomputed domains. Arbitrary-array cases use arbitrary host values throughout and freeze their input representation, memory layout, ordering and branch distribution. An adverse case uses the admissible value of a producer-controlled choice that minimizes N relative to C within q's semantics. Every case form whose I includes arrived host arrays requires the most compact representation q admits (factored axes or broadcast operands where I is product-structured, binary64, no conversion or indirection), in dense, contiguous, unit-stride layout, as a saturated adverse case at every required population. Alternating-interior cases alternate across the entire occupied domain. Tile-capacity cases freeze occupancy and partial-tail layout at each required crossing rather than averaging it into full tiles. For value maps, decisions, aggregates and first/last forms, freeze the output/quantifier semantics and match-position distribution, including a full-scan case wherever applicable; deterministic analytic shortcuts remain available to N. For any inherited form not explicitly described here, its defining requirement supplies the predicate that every occupied selection must satisfy, with the complete construction recorded and independently reviewed before collection.

**Rule (Independent review before collection)** · `rule:nrz:lc-overhead-precollection-review`

Before any acceptance collection, independently review and freeze the complete manifest, case constructions, source records, machine configuration and pin/admit choice, graph inventories, predictions, sensitivity cases and observation/statistical settings. This review checks every item in (`def:nrz:lc-overhead-naive`) and does not replace the blocking final review under (`rule:nrz:lc-closing-independent-review`). Unresolved findings block collection. Retain the reviewed manifest digest with every run; changed choices require a newly reviewed manifest and fresh complete observations under (`rule:nrz:lc-overhead-verdict`).

The review explicitly checks remaining producer-controlled choices that could raise N or lower C or otherwise favour any acceptance test in (`dec:nrz:lc-overhead-intervals`), (`dec:nrz:lc-overhead-remainder-limit`), (`rule:nrz:lc-overhead-verdict`): input generators and seeds, input representation and memory layout of arrived host arrays (stride, record width, alignment, padding, indirection), operand magnitudes and exceptional classes, support widths and correlation structure, refinement precision/depth and unchanged resource limits, fallback fraction, reuse lifetimes and cache state, tile partition/occupancy and ordering, first/last match placement, sample/branch/output extents, output consumption, compiler/build and arithmetic policies, phase core allotments with a justification of the chosen p_h, core affinity, competing load, run ordering, sampler count/stopping rules, and the boundaries between setup, steady state, finish and harness work. Any producer-controlled choice that can raise N or lower C or otherwise favours any acceptance test in (`dec:nrz:lc-overhead-intervals`), (`dec:nrz:lc-overhead-remainder-limit`), (`rule:nrz:lc-overhead-verdict`) is in scope whether listed or not; review must identify and justify such choices and their required adverse cases under (`def:nrz:lc-overhead-case-makeup`). A producer-controlled choice found at closing review that the reviewed manifest did not identify, freeze and cover with its required adverse cases invalidates every run under that manifest digest; (`claim:nrz:lc-closing-overhead-bound`) remains unmet until a newly reviewed manifest and complete recollection. Freeze each choice with a semantic or source-backed justification and required adverse cases before seeing acceptance data; reject favorable seed searches, convenient severity choices, selective outputs, scope shifts and outcome-dependent stopping or reruns. Node-chosen runtime partitions and routes retain their frozen selection policy and actual receipts rather than imposing an engine default. The independent review must justify coverage and any scope limitation; freezing an arbitrary favorable choice alone does not establish completeness. Limits, defaults and pins of the engine remain unchanged.

**Rule (Departures and verdict)** · `rule:nrz:lc-overhead-verdict`

Before measuring, record each component's predicted operation vector, source-backed time/range, resource binding, numerical-law proof and assumptions. Predicted time ranges may be only the minimum-to-maximum envelope of the frozen theta sensitivity cases applied to the frozen graph, assignment and scope; each case requires a named source or an explicit derivation from stated premises, and no fitted margin or post-observation widening is allowed. Compare exact operation receipts exactly to path-conditioned predictions; a time departure means that the measured interval and prior predicted range do not overlap (a shared endpoint counts as overlap). For each independently identifiable component in each run, use a two-sided 95% percentile bootstrap interval of its measured time slope, with the paired row resampling and frozen resample count of (`dec:nrz:lc-overhead-intervals`), without adjustment for m; departure tests are separate from the m acceptance comparisons. Sensitivity sources and derivations require independent review under (`def:nrz:lc-overhead-naive`); unsupported low efficiencies cannot widen the predicted range. For fused constituents lacking an identifiable interval, report unresolved attribution rather than an apparent agreement; retain differences in seconds and normalized by N. Any departure requires a causal explanation supported by receipts and source/lowering evidence, including changed binding resources, occupancy, fallback or cache behavior. An unexplained departure, incomplete observation, unresolved fused attribution, missing source coefficient, nonpositive denominator, unmet stability assumption, partial run or an invalidated manifest under (`rule:nrz:lc-overhead-precollection-review`) prevents acceptance even if R_hat is small. Failure of the observed-row guard in (`dec:nrz:lc-overhead-intervals`) prevents acceptance. A ratio interval with upper endpoint above 10.0 is not accepted; if its lower endpoint is above 10.0 report a demonstrated excess, otherwise report inconclusive evidence. Fixes require a new versioned prediction/manifest and fresh complete acceptance observations, preserving prior failures; do not fit N, loosen tolerances or selectively rerun favorable rows. An explained budget above eight remains a reported budget risk, never an automatic satisfaction of the predicted-budget claim. Report the early cold-case budget at the smallest dense K at or above ten, including exact construction and pi evidence, as a risk to both the predicted budget and the bound where indicated; a small-population excess is not waived.

## Concept resolutions and retained decisions · `sec:nrz:lc-overhead-resolutions`

**Decision (Composition and attribution resolution)** · `dec:nrz:lc-overhead-concept-resolution`

The accounting part of (`open:nrz:lc-compute-composition`) is resolved by (`def:nrz:lc-overhead-resource`), (`rule:nrz:lc-overhead-composition`): sum shared resource demand inside phases and add sequential phase time. Numerical enclosure proofs and exact-recipe schedules remain prerequisites under (`req:nrz:lc-overhead-runs`), not presumed facts. (`open:nrz:lc-compute-attribution`) is resolved by the actual-consumer allocation and separate K,E,n scopes of (`rule:nrz:lc-overhead-scopes`). (`open:nrz:lc-compute-observability`) is resolved as an implementation contract by (`req:nrz:lc-overhead-map`), (`req:nrz:lc-overhead-additions`) and the frozen protocol in (`sec:nrz:lc-overhead-acceptance`); the intrinsic fused-time limitation is retained below. These decisions do not promote design contracts to executable evidence.

**Open Question (Reference machine source completion)** · `open:nrz:lc-overhead-machine-decision`

The arithmetic part of (`open:nrz:lc-compute-machine-evidence`) has the source mapping in (`obs:nrz:lc-overhead-amd-arithmetic`). The remaining blocking source decision is to establish comparison, mask/integer and mixed-pipe schedules, confirm the inferred column interpretation and operand applicability for acceptance, and supply a documented traffic/controller model or theoretical efficiency assumptions with a named source or an explicit derivation from stated premises for the chosen sustainable bandwidth. Sustainable bandwidth remains an assumption, not a value supplied by the workbook. The repository does not select Intel, Arm or another vendor’s reference record here; vendor/family choice, conflicting table interpretations and applicability must be settled and frozen under (`def:nrz:lc-overhead-source-record`) before accepting that instance. The concept's illustrative quarter/three-quarter bandwidth efficiencies and 4.25–8.5 conditional arithmetic case are not acceptance coefficients. Engineering merit cannot turn absent documentary evidence into a number. A fully documented parameter range may remain conditional for exploration; an unconditional verdict must use the smallest N over every admitted theta and report all sensitivity cases, with the same certified machine/load applicability. The ceiling rule covers every machine parameter that affects speed, including core clock, configured memory transfer rate and channel population, fabric clock, cache and port rates, instruction resources and the matched phase core allotment in (`def:nrz:lc-overhead-resource`). Apply (`rule:nrz:lc-overhead-host-configuration`) throughout the manifest. A configured speed exceeding a documented ceiling must be included with a justified rate derivation or leave the machine decision unresolved; it cannot be ignored in favor of a slower denominator. The admitted theta set always includes the documented reference values and the higher of documented and configured values for each speed parameter; a degraded configured value never replaces the reference. It includes the transfer-rate ceiling at efficiency 1 for each relevant bandwidth level, derived from those reference and higher resources with their documented topology and traffic constraints; lower efficiencies are sensitivity cases requiring a named source or explicit derivation, and cannot replace or exclude that ceiling. Retain the compatibility justification for the admitted configurations and their speed ceilings. Completeness of the parameters and admissibility of sensitivity cases require the independent review in (`def:nrz:lc-overhead-naive`). Minimize N over this set and optimal eligible-pipe assignments even when a slower assumption would improve the ratio. If no positive justified lower N exists, only conditional predictions can be published.

**Rule (One acceptance host configuration)** · `rule:nrz:lc-overhead-host-configuration`

Freeze one acceptance configuration and one choice between pin and admit for the whole manifest before collection, under (`rule:nrz:lc-overhead-precollection-review`); no (q,I), scope or run may select a different configuration to improve its ratio. Every speed parameter is at or above the reference node's documented operating point: core clock at least the 3.4 GHz base in (`fact:nrz:lc-compute-machine`), every documented memory channel populated at no less than DDR4-3200 under (`fact:nrz:lc-compute-machine`), and fabric clock at least the documented default. Record exact source rows for channel topology and fabric default under (`def:nrz:lc-overhead-source-record`); the reference channel count remains unresolved until its topology source row is supplied, and absent documentary support leaves the machine decision unresolved, not a producer-selected lower default. A lower configured speed or missing channel is not an acceptance host without a named amendment to this design. Phase core allotments follow (`def:nrz:lc-overhead-resource`), not the node's total cores.

The pin option fixes the reviewed model clock and memory configuration at or above those reference values and disables boost. For every run retain a boost-off reading, an effective-frequency counter covering the run, and the per-run memory configuration including channel population and transfer rate, together with fabric configuration and provenance. Document counter semantics and resolution sufficient to detect excursions, not merely a frequency-limit setting or an average that conceals boost; an unverifiable or failed pin check invalidates the run. These readings check the pin and do not calibrate theta or substitute counter-derived rates into N. The admit option includes the highest documented clock including boost and the higher of documented and configured values for every speed parameter, with per-run configuration evidence confirming the frozen setup. Both options retain the reference values and required ceilings in (`open:nrz:lc-overhead-machine-decision`); a change of option or configuration requires a newly reviewed manifest and complete recollection.

**Open Question (Individual times inside fused kernels)** · `open:nrz:lc-overhead-fused-attribution`

Elapsed time is observable for a fused kernel, but a unique elapsed duration for its interleaved center, radius, rounding, comparisons, in-kernel mask packing and output stores is not. Separate counters and a joint time give an honest resource test, not the register's independent component times. Before claiming complete tracking, obtain an independently reviewed attribution method with an explicit identifiable observable and uncertainty, preserving the ordinary fused execution, or resolve the register's interpretation of grouped time evidence through its owning design. This design does not authorize weakening that claim or de-fusing the acceptance workload to manufacture separability. Until then report constituent times as unresolved and leave tracking and bound claims unmet under (`rule:nrz:lc-overhead-verdict`).

**Decision (Concept review corrections)** · `dec:nrz:lc-overhead-review-corrections`

The conditional factor in (`pred:nrz:lc-compute-overhead-envelope`) explicitly requires separate execution resources, adding shared-pipe mask/integer demand to floating demand instead. Its unsupported illustrative population sentence is removed; the symbolic tile allowance remains. The conditional local case above eightfold is stated in (`pred:nrz:lc-compute-overhead-envelope`), cited by (`tab:nrz:lc-closing-certification-cost`). The energy intermediate in (`calc:nrz:lc-compute-energy`) is e2, reserving h for the predicate threshold. The concept and its template carry these corrections together without changing a closing status.
